<version>1.0.0</version>
<language>Rust</language>
Output src/relativity.rs; manual prompt-first implementation, no provider regeneration claim.
Reusable Lorentz metric/vector/boost capabilities, time first, metric diag(-1,1,1,1).
Rapidity holds finite eta; from_beta rejects nonfinite or |beta|>=1; beta returns
error when tanh rounds to +/-1 (no clamping). Addition rejects overflow.
Boost convention: L00=cosh eta, L0i=Li0=ni sinh eta,
Lij=deltaij+ni nj (cosh eta-1). Axis explicitly validates unit length against
finite tolerance <=1e-6, never normalizes. Compute cosh-1=2 sinh(eta/2)^2
for tiny eta. Reject all nonfinite inputs/results, including diagnostic overflow.
Numerical diagnostics expose absolute and scaled residuals, scale and declared
absolute/relative tolerances; never assert floating point Lorentz exactness.
Generic Coefficient exact metric/raise/lower/dot/apply reuse Budget and checked
matrix operations. Validate inputs before cloning; deterministic budget failures.
Exact axial rational boosts accept BigQ u=tanh(eta/2), |u|<1. Compute c=(1+u²)/(1-u²)
and s=2u/(1-u²) with checked BigQ then BigC; no rational eta assertion.
Symbolic axial boost uses BigPoly labels c,s, returning matrix AND explicit
condition polynomial c²-s²-1=0. Distinct nonempty labels; checked constructors
and polynomial arithmetic only; no transcendental parser or copied algorithms.
Public API and tolerance semantics documented in docs/RELATIVITY.md.
Independent tests cover sign/frame control, metric, inverse, interval, composition,
3-4-5 rational boost, symbolic condition, tiny eta, invalid axis/beta/nonfinite,
budget failure and overflow. Legacy files and mono-notes MUST remain untouched.
